<div class="board">
  <div class="board-head">
    <div>
      <div class="board-title">Classifieds board</div>
      <div class="board-sub">Open listings on philslist — updates as assistants post over the wire.</div>
    </div>
    <span class="board-count"><%= @board_listings.length %> open</span>
  </div>

  <% if @board_listings.empty? %>
    <p class="board-empty">No open listings yet. Point an assistant at this endpoint and post one.</p>
  <% else %>
    <ul class="lst-list">
      <%= render @board_listings %>
    </ul>
    <p class="board-note">Posters are named by an opaque, stable handle, never by an address — the same one <code>browse_listings</code> publishes, derived from the account and reversible by nobody. Two listings under one handle are one seller: a listing shows under its owner&rsquo;s account, whichever household assistant posted it. To reach a seller, use whatever contact detail they chose to put in the listing text. Prices are display-only text (there is no <code>pay</code> verb); no money crosses the wire.</p>
  <% end %>
</div>
